{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "977b366d-cb2b-8651-a417-c79749c15445",
  "created_at": "2026-02-19T13:48:24-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Thomas Tillinghast",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:16-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:20-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, hello. Um, I am calling about my water bill. It is, uh, very big this time. Almost double. I do not understand why."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:29-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure, let's take a look. Can I get the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:34-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Three forty-six Callender Avenue. In the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Callender Avenue. And your name on the account?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:42-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thomas Tillinghast. I rent there, the, the apartment. The bill comes to me, I think."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:48-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, Mr. Tillinghast, I've got it up. Do you have the paper bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:45:55-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I have it here in my hand. One moment. [pause] The date on top says, uh, February the second. Two thousand twenty-six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's the bill date. And what's the amount due on yours?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:08-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It says, um, one hundred, eighty-six dollars. Before it was ninety, maybe ninety-five. Always about this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:14-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. Looking at the account, the last reading is higher than the one before it, so it's billing you for more usage. Sometimes that's a leak, like a running toilet, or just a longer billing period."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:27-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A running toilet. Is that, the water goes, goes all the time in the bowl?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:33-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, it keeps trickling into the bowl even when nobody flushed. You can drop some food coloring in the tank and see if it shows up in the bowl after a while."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:44-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Food coloring. I will try. And on the bill there is a word, I do not know. Is it, um, \"consumption\"? It sounds like another word, \"consumption\", \"assumption\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:46:54-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, that's the one. Consumption, C-O-N-S-U-M-P-T-I-O-N. It just means how much water you used. Assumption with an A is a different word altogether."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:02-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah. C, O, N, S, U, M, P, T, I, O, N. Okay. Consumption. So the number here is how much I used, not what I pay."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:12-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Exactly. Usage is one number, and the dollars come after that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:17-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see, I see. Now, I want to pay before the weekend. But the office, it closes, yes? How can I pay when it is closed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:26-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. You can pay online any time through the city website, and there's a payment drop box outside City Hall you can use after hours. Or there's an automated phone line too, if you have your account number handy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:40-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The box. Outside, I put a check, in the box?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:44-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, a check with your account number written on it. Don't put cash in there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:50-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No cash. Okay. And the account number, it is on the bill, no?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:47:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's on the bill, near the top right. Should be a long number under the date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:48:01-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, yes, I see it. Okay. I will check the toilet first, and then pay. If the number is still big, I call again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:48:10-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Absolutely. If it keeps running high, we can send someone to check the meter. Just call back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:48:16-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Tony. I think I understand. Mostly. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-19T13:48:20-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, Mr. Tillinghast. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
